Date:     Tue, 28 Dec 93 9:41:25 EST
From: cards@top.cis.syr.edu
Subject: Why have children?

Another nontraditional family arrangement was tried by the
Oneida Community in upstate New York back in the 1800's.
All but the most personal property was communal (yuck),
and all adult males were married to all adult females.
Children were regarded as 'belonging' to the community
vs their specific parents (hard to identify the father
in any event).  They weren't much on sex, though, and
basically died out.  Their few descendants reorganized
along more traditonal lines as good capitalists: the
world-famous Oneida Silversmiths company.
